{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1503224-mixed-talent-and-nova-games","id":1503224,"title":"Mixed Talent and Nova Games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-16T04:27:44-08:00","id":1503224,"title":"Mixed Talent and Nova Games?","content":"Hey I was wondering if anyone had any experience runnning or playing in mixed groups of Talents and Novas? I'm trying to get my Exalted group to switch to Storypath after our current campaign and my ST has been interested in doing supers but hasn't liked more well known/popular other supers system, but he has also asked about doing Batman and Hawkeye type characters which I'm pretty sure would be Talents but don't know how well they would stack up and mix with Novas in the same group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T05:23:21-08:00","id":1503228,"title":"","content":"My understanding is novas tend to be very, very good at one or a few things. Talents can be pretty darn good at lots of things. One Talent Gift you'll want to encourage is The Bigger They Are, which helps negate Scale differences between the Talent and any Novas they may be dealing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T06:24:08-08:00","id":1503233,"title":"","content":"I honestly would make Batman, Hawkeye and other &quot;hyper trained fellows&quot; as Talents, and you can play them in the same game as Florin described, BUT, you can easily stat them as Novas.<br /> <br /> Give guys like Hawkeye the Acuracy mega edge, Batman can have Mega Mental powers and Blackwidow Mega Social (tricking someone to think they are actually torturing her when she is in fact spying on them) and try to stay on lower levels of mega attributes (specially Mega Might, that is the most obvious).<br /> <br /> There is even a name for this kind of character in universe in Aberrant, they are called Darkstars, Novas that have subtle powers that seams to work as hyper capable people or at least not obvious enough to be pointed as Novas at first glance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T06:34:13-08:00","id":1503234,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the insight guys and I knew about darkstars and that they could do some of that lifting too, but also know some people still aren't always statisfied with that because they really just want to be the super exceptional baseline. However it will definitely something I suggest for those concepts if I get them to go with an Aberrant game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T07:49:39-08:00","id":1503238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1503224-mixed-talent-and-nova-games?p=1503228#post1503228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is novas tend to be very, very good at one or a few things. Talents can be pretty darn good at lots of things. One Talent Gift you'll want to encourage is The Bigger They Are, which helps negate Scale differences between the Talent and any Novas they may be dealing with.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason why The Bigger They Are appears in TC:Aberrant; it's almost but not quite a requirement for Talents who are having to deal with a world filled with Novas.<br /> <br /> You may also want to lean heavily into the Super-Science rules, possibly even investing in an Edge that gives your Talent appropriate signature gear: Batman's utility belt and Hawkeye's trick arrows. They're as close to \u201chaving Quantum Powers\u201d as a Talent is going to get. Grant Morrison mentioned when he was revitalizing the JLA in the late 90s that in order for Batman to keep pace with the rest of the League, he needed to lean heavily on the sci-fi aspects of the character, such as the Batplane and the miscellaneous gadgetry he carries around with him. Also bear in mind that Inspired Super-Science can do a lot more than most people give it credit for: Mr. Freeze's ice gun can be built using Inspired Super-Science. <br /> <br /> Do that, but also remember that the main advantage that Talents have over Novas is that they have access to Dramatic Editing \u201cfor free\u201d (as opposed to how Novas need to take a Mega-Edge to access it). It's up to you whether you want to play that off as retroactive prep-work or just lucky breaks; the mechanics are the same either way. That said, if you have access to either Adventure or Assassins, you might want to make things even easier for the Talents by using the enhanced DE rules that daredevils and assassins have access to. In particular, both get to pay less to use DE, and also have the option of spending Momentum rather than Inspiration (albeit at a 2:1 exchange rate).<br /> <br /> There are also other options available like making Dramatic Editing available through stunting instead of spending Inspiration (again, I think it's a 2:1 exchange rate, with 2 successes on an appropriate Stunt buying one Inspiration worth of DE); though that's more suitable for representing exceptional competence than lucky breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-16-2023, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T10:30:05-08:00","id":1503247,"title":"","content":"Thanks I'll look into what they have in Assassin's as I currently only have Core, Aeon, Aberrant and Assassins","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:31:32-08:00","id":1503259,"title":"","content":"I think there are two big problems with running a talent in a Nova game. First is that Novas receive 150 xp as part of the character creation process while Talents get four Gifts and some Edge dots. Simply granting a Talent the same xp will leave them bloated with Gifts, which can overwhelm a new player. Second is that Novas roll against 7 while Talents roll against 8, meaning every Skill+Attribute roll is easier for the Nova, before figuring in Mega-Attributes.<br /> <br /> I'd just build a Batman/Hawkeye type as a Nova with Quantum 1 (free) + a few dots in Nova traits, then spend the bulk of their starting xp on Paths and Attributes. A fair number of mundane Edges are quite similar to Nova traits and cost less xp (or come free as part of their Paths). For example, Swift (one dot, core book) gets you speed scale for running, Strongman (three dots, Aether manuscript) gets you Might scale, and Striking (two dots, core book) gets you a conditional bonus to Social rolls that is equivalent to the bonus from scale. They won't have the massive raw power of many PC Novas, but they'll be reasonably good at practically everything, can mow down minions while their allies take on the enemy big hitters, and are a consistent source of teamwork bonuses for any allies they assist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}